     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi,</div><div><br></div><div>I noticed that Subread 1.6.3 no longer builds the executable coverageCount. Was this intentional? There is no mention in the <a href=\"http://subread.sourceforge.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://subread.sourceforge.net/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234216465000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3j7f5sO009Cnub-umMuICB\">changelog</a> that this feature was deprecated. Also, I couldn&#39;t find anything when I <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/subread/coverageCount%7Csort:date\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!searchin/subread/coverageCount%257Csort:date&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234216465000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1g-lW_CmtC5chQHPL5YYqF\">searched the mailing list for coverageCount</a>.</div><div><br></div><div>Here are the steps I took to verify this:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">docker run -it --rm ubuntu<br>apt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#008\">get</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> update<br>apt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#008\">get</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> install -y gcc make wget zlib1g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dev<br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># 1.6.2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><br><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">wget https</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//<a href=\"http://downloads.sourceforge.net/project/subread/subread-1.6.2/subread-1.6.2-source.tar.gz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&am